# Data and licence rules

## Sources and required attribution

| Source | Licence | Attribution text |
|---|---|---|
| Open Food Facts product API v2 | ODbL 1.0 | "Data from Open Food Facts (openfoodfacts.org), ODbL" |
| openFDA food enforcement | Public domain / CC0 | Say the project is not endorsed by the FDA. |
| UK FSA food alerts | Open Government Licence v3.0 | "Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0" |

Evidence records carry the source URL and the licence string.

## What may be committed

- Committed data: `data/reference/market_allergens.json` (each entry with statute, edition and citation URL) and `data/manifest/skus.json` (GTIN, market, reference labels).
- Never commit bulk Open Food Facts data, Open Food Facts ingredient text, or raw API dumps. Everything else under `data/` is runtime state and stays gitignored.
- The US tree-nut list is transcribed from FDA's food-allergen guidance (Edition 5) page, with its URL, not typed from memory.
- Evaluation labels are "reference labels" derived from recalls and documented label rules. Never call them "hand-labelled".
- No personal data: firm street addresses are never selected, and no Open Food Facts contributor fields are read.

## Code and model licences

- The project is Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE`, `NOTICE`).
- Meterless engines are Apache-2.0 and vendored unchanged; keep their `LICENSE` files and the entry in `NOTICE`.
- Code adapted from the Zetaris getting-started repository (Apache-2.0) keeps an attribution header in the file and gets an entry in `NOTICE`.
- NVIDIA Nemotron is used under the NVIDIA Open Model License. Model weights are never added to the repository.
